只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Fix and diagnose DeepSeek Harness on native Windows. Official PowerShell, Workspace Write, shortcuts, and legacy preset repair. No WSL.","id":"gh:1334876923","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-win32","slug":"sjh9714/dsh-win32","topics":["ai-agent","deepseek","deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","deepseek-v4","doctor","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","native-windows","no-wsl","powershell","sandbox","win32","windows","windows-fix","workspace-write"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Fix and diagnose DeepSeek Harness on native Windows. Official PowerShell, Workspace Write, shortcuts"},{"id":"p1s2","text":", and legacy preset repair. No WSL."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-win32"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"## Fix DSH on Windows. No WSL."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Official PowerShell. Workspace Write. One command.**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Current DeepSeek Harness already includes persistent PowerShell and a Windows ACL sandbox. dsh-win32"},{"id":"p6s2","text":" checks that official stack, finds known Windows failures, applies the repairs it can prove safe, an"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"d creates a desktop shortcut."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"It does not install Git, PowerShell, busybox, WSL, or another DSH bundle on the current path."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Use the standalone CLI above on current DSH. Do **not** run `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-win32`"},{"id":"p8s2","text":" for this workflow: that installs the legacy bundle, not the current Windows setup path."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"中文 · Windows evidence and legacy details"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Using a coding agent? Copy the setup and verification request. For a guided walkthrough, see Windows"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" troubleshooting in Chinese."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Start with the Windows first-run walkthrough if DSH will not launch or a check fails. It follows one"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" problem from diagnosis through the next verification step. Share your first-run result, including a"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ttempts that are still blocked."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**Need to disable or uninstall the old plugin, even when DSH cannot start?** See disable / uninstall"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" / remove. From 0.17.14, `npx dsh-win32@0.17.14 disable --profile web` previews offline deactivation"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"; after stopping DSH, add `--apply` to back up the manifest and disconnect only the old bundle."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## See the current setup"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**Reproduced setup flow. This is not a screen recording.**"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The command checks the official persistent PowerShell and Workspace Write packages, creates the shor"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"tcut, and leaves the profile on the stock Minimal preset."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## What setup does"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- Checks the latest published DSH Windows package contract\n- Checks PowerShell 7 and known broken ko"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"ffi runtimes\n- Creates a `DeepSeek Harness` desktop shortcut for the Web profile\n- Leaves the offici"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"al profile and preset unchanged\n- Shows the exact next steps for a first session"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"After setup, open DSH, add a workspace, choose the stock **Minimal** preset, and keep **Workspace Wr"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"pen DSH, add a workspace, choose the stock **Minimal** preset, and keep **Workspace Write** enabled."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Use another profile without creating a shortcut."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"`--sandboxed` remains accepted for old notes and scripts. Current DSH already provides the sandbox, "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"so the flag makes no extra change."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Live verification of an installed stack"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"From **0.17.12**, opt in to setup followed by one installed-stack check:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Use `--profile NAME --no-shortcut` when appropriate. Ordinary `setup` is unchanged; `--legacy --veri"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"fy` is rejected. Setup and component acceptance are reported separately, and a failed or unsupported"},{"id":"p25s3","text":" verification makes the command exit nonzero. This does not install DSH or prove a complete Desktop/"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"Minimal session. For a check without setup or JSON output, use the standalone command:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"`verify` is a model- and API-key-free acceptance run against an **already installed** `@deepseek-ai/"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"dsh` dependency tree. It does not use registry metadata as proof. In an isolated temporary home and "},{"id":"p27s3","text":"workspace it invokes the installed model-facing persistent `pwsh` tool through the official terminal"},{"id":"p27s4","text":", subprocess, Workspace Write policy, and Windows ACL sandbox components."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"A pass requires all of these live observations:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- 64-bit PowerShell 7 launches and reports a real executable\n- two `pwsh` calls retain the same PTY,"},{"id":"p29s2","text":" current directory, and environment state\n- exact content is written and read inside the temporary w"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"orkspace\n- a normal-process control can write the isolated outside target, while confined PowerShell"},{"id":"p29s4","text":" is denied and creates no file\n- the shell recovers after denial; cancellation tears down its PTY; a"},{"id":"p29s5","text":" replacement call works; and a second cancellation tears down cleanly\n- every runtime resource, temp"},{"id":"p29s6","text":"orary home, and temporary workspace is removed"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"No user DSH profile, config, workspace, or PowerShell profile is loaded or changed. Secret-bearing e"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"nvironment variables are not passed to the worker, and reports contain no tested paths or terminal o"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"utput. Native Windows and a DSH-supported Node release are required; Node 23 is explicitly unsupport"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"ut. Native Windows and a DSH-supported Node release are required; Node 23 is explicitly unsupported."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"If a timeout or output limit leaves worker or descendant containment unconfirmed, verification fails"},{"id":"p31s2","text":" and preserves the isolated snapshot instead of deleting files under a potentially live process."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Doctor and safe repair"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"`doctor` verifies the published DSH Windows package contract and checks local Windows failures. Its "},{"id":"p35s2","text":"JSON output follows the `dsh-doctor/v1` envelope. Use `verify` when you need live evidence from the "},{"id":"p35s3","text":"installed stack rather than registry metadata."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"`fix` only repairs installed koffi versions that are known broken or fail a real runtime load. It ve"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"rifies the load again after repair."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"## Check an upgrade before you run it"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"`preflight` answers one question: can this profile move to that DSH version? It is read-only and als"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"o runs on macOS and Linux. `--target` takes an exact version or a dist-tag of `@deepseek-ai/dsh` and"},{"id":"p39s3","text":" defaults to `latest`."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"- **Plugins.** It reads the third-party plugins in the profile, including disabled ones, and applies"},{"id":"p40s2","text":" the host's own rule to the target: `engines.dsh` decides alone when present, otherwise the DSH peer"},{"id":"p40s3","text":"s must match, and prereleases count. CI compares this judgment with the installed `dsh-app-boot`. An"},{"id":"p40s4","text":" exemption from `dsh plugin allow-version` counts only if it names the exact target.\n- **Node.** It "},{"id":"p40s5","text":"uses the target's `engines.node`. Some releases declare none, so it then falls back to `^22.19.0 || "},{"id":"p40s6","text":">=24` and says so.\n- **Windows.** It checks that PowerShell 7 exists and that `pwsh` resolves throug"},{"id":"p40s7","text":"o.\n- **Windows.** It checks that PowerShell 7 exists and that `pwsh` resolves through PATH.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"## Upstream plugin and hook boundaries"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"Two current DSH control paths sit outside repairs that dsh-win32 can safely apply:"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"## Bring an existing setup"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
